            "attachment_title": "Public Notices French - Hybrid Standing Committee.pdf"
          }
        ],
        "description": "Notices and meeting information are attached to the agenda and minutes, including: availability of simultaneous interpretation and accessibility accommodations; in camera meeting procedures; information items not subject to discussion; personal information disclaimer for correspondents and public speakers; notices regarding minutes; and remote participation details.\nAccessible formats and communication supports are available, upon request.\nExcept where otherwise indicated, reports requiring Council consideration will be presented to Council on Wednesday, May 14, 2025 in Planning and Housing Committee Report 46.\nThe deadline to register by phone to speak, or submit written comments or visual presentations is 4 pm on Tuesday, May 6, 2025, and the deadline to register by email to speak is 8:30 am on Wednesday, May 7, 2025.",
        "minutes": "This is a public meeting to consider the proposed Comprehensive Official Plan and Zoning By-law Amendments listed as Item(s) 5.1 on today\u2019s Agenda.\nFor the items just mentioned, only those specifically identified in the Planning Act who make oral submissions today or written submissions before the amendments are adopted may appeal the matter to the Ontario Land Tribunal. In addition, the applicant may appeal the matter to the Ontario Land Tribunal if Council does not adopt an amendment within 90 days of receipt of the application for a Zoning By-law Amendment and 120 days for an Official Plan Amendment.\nTo submit written comments on these amendments, prior to their consideration by City Council on May 14, 2025, please email or call the Committee or Council Coordinator.",
        "motions": []
